// src/v4/std/float.dag
//
// Scope: IEEE-754 binary floating-point — reals as the hardware defines
//        them. Deliberately separate from integer: floating-point
//        arithmetic is NOT a clean algebra (rounding breaks associativity;
//        NaN breaks reflexive equality), so it is modeled honestly as the
//        hardware artifact rather than grounded in the algebra roots.
// Anchor: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEEE_754
//
// Owns:
//   - Float — IEEE-754 binary floating-point (Float32 / Float64). The one
//     genuine opaque/irreducible scalar in this layer: it does not
//     decompose into the algebra roots; its semantics are hardware-defined.
//   - Tier-2 totalization for the partial / non-total operations
//     (NaN-producing ops; ordering in the presence of NaN) — STRUCTURE.md
//     commitment #2
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag
//   - std/machine.dag: the bit-width (Float32 / Float64)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-3 (scalar/numeric stack). Replaces
//   part of the deleted std/primitive.dag; see src/v4/STRUCTURE.md
//   §"scalar/numeric concept decomposition".
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.std.float
